  "repository_intelligence": {
    "purpose": "Multi-client plugin and instruction distributions for Zapier's hosted MCP service, with onboarding, role-based action discovery, status auditing and confirmation-aware SaaS action guidance; no hosted server implementation is present.",
    "reuse_recommendation": "Install the appropriate client package and authenticate only the required actions; host instructions do not replace server authorization.",
    "inspection_scope": "Complete 29-file tree: four skills, a specialist agent, client distribution manifests, shared remote MCP connector configuration and an always-applied lifecycle rule. Claude/Codex/Cursor/GitHub/Gemini/Kiro packaging and steering variants wrap the same hosted service and role contracts; do not invent local MCP server/tool implementations for its external app catalogue. Repository-level completion only; detailed entities are preserved unchanged.",
    "license_notes": "MIT; source-specific notices remain applicable.",
    "runtime": [
      "Markdown skills/agent rules",
      "JSON MCP/client manifests",
      "Remote HTTP MCP service"
    ],
    "keywords": [
      "Zapier",
      "MCP client",
      "OAuth",
      "SaaS actions",
      "workflow automation",
      "confirmation",
      "connector"
    ],
    "risk_notes": [
      "Remote OAuth and user-enabled actions determine real access; no server authorization implementation is present to audit here. The agent/rule explicitly require a user-approved shown payload for writes and prohibit third-party content from granting approval. These are instruction contracts, not server-enforced access controls. The explore skill's assumption of broad app support must be checked against actual configured actions. Credentials, MCP transport, app reads/writes and client reloads were not exercised during this static census."
    ],
